<title>UK: SOCCER-UEFA CUP THIRD ROUND, SECOND LEG RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-UEFA CUP THIRD ROUND, SECOND LEG RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of UEFA Cup third round,</p>
<p>second leg soccer matches on Tuesday:</p>
<p>In Karlsruhe: Karlsruhe (Germany) 0 Brondby (Denmark) 5</p>
<p>(halftime 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers: Ruben Bagger 41, Dan Eggen 43, Kim Vilfort 59,</p>
<p>Peter Moeller 74, 81</p>
<p>Attendance: 21,000</p>
<p>Brondby won 6-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Gelsenkirchen: Schalke (Germany) 2 Club Brugge (Belgium)</p>
<p>0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Martin Max (9), Youri Mulder (90)</p>
<p>Attendance: 51,000</p>
<p>Schalke win 3-2 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Istanbul: Besiktas (Turkey) 2 Valencia (Spain) 2 (2-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Besiktas - Serdar Topraktepe (16), Oktay Derelioglu (45 pen)</p>
<p>Valencia - Claudio Lopez (24), Goran Vlaovic (44)</p>
<p>Valencia win 5-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Brussels: Anderlecht (Belgium) 1 Helsingborg (Sweden) 0</p>
<p>(0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Johan Walem (68)</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,000</p>
<p>Anderlecht won 1-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Rotterdam: Feyenoord (Netherlands) 2 Tenerife (Spain) 4</p>
<p>(0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Feyenoord - Pablo Sanchez 82, Henk Vos 87</p>
<p>Tenerife - Felipe 5, Juanele 45, 60, Pablo Paz 74</p>
<p>Tenerife win 4-2 on aggregate  MORE kl</p>
<p>In Hamburg: Hamburg (Germany) 0 Monaco 2 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Viktor Ikpeba 62, Ali Bernabia 88 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Monaco win 5-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Oporto, Portugal:  Boavista (Portugal) 0 Internazionale Milan (Italy) 2 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: Youri Djorkaeff 12 penalty, Paul Ince 66.</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,500</p>
<p>Inter win 7-1 on aggregate  </p>
<p>In Newcastle: Newcastle United (England) 2 Metz (France) 0</p>
<p>(0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Faustino Asprilla 80, 82</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,641</p>
<p>Newcastle win 3-1 on aggregate.</p>
<p>In Hamburg: Hamburg (Germany) 0 Monaco 2 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Viktor Ikpeba 62, Ali Bernabia 88 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Monaco win 5-0 on aggregate</p>
</text>
